[SWS_LBAP_00065] Bitfield Data Type
⌈
Kind:
class
Header file:
#include "{<ns-derived-dir-path>}/impl_type_{<shortname-lower>}.h"
Scope:
namespace {<cppidt-ns-list-lc>}
Symbol:
{<cppidt-sn>}
Syntax:
class {<cppidt-sn>} {...};
Description:
there shall exist a C++ class declaration representing a bitfield.
For each:
• StdCppImplementationDataType. category ==TYPE_REFERENCE which type-resolves
to a
• StdCppImplementationDataType. category ==VALUE, and that aggregates a
• StdCppImplementationDataType. swDataDefProps. compuMethod. category
==BITFIELD_TEXTTABLE
Descriptors:
{<cppidt-sn>}
as per {<symbol-string>} in [SWS_LBAP_00015]
Example:
// Example: Bitfield / CompuMethod.category=BITFIELD_TEXTTABLE
class TirePressure {
public:
// COMPU-SCALE=frontLeft
// MASK=0b00000001
using frontLeft
= ara::core::Bitset<1>;
...
// COMPU-SCALE=problem
// MASK=0b00110000
using problem
= ara::core::Bitset<2>;
...
[[nodiscard]] frontLeft Get_frontLeft() const noexcept;
// SYMBOL=frontLeft_no
TirePressure& Set_frontLeft_no();
// [0]
// SYMBOL=frontLeft_yes
TirePressure& Set_frontLeft_yes();
// [1]
...
[[nodiscard]] problem Get_problem() const noexcept;
// SYMBOL=problem_flat_tire
TirePressure& Set_problem_flat_tire();
// [0,0]
// SYMBOL=problem_low_pressure
TirePressure& Set_problem_low_pressure();// [0,1]
// SYMBOL=problem_unbalanced
TirePressure& Set_problem_unbalanced();
// [1,0]
// SYMBOL=problem_unknown
TirePressure& Set_problem_unknown();
// [1,1]
};
▽ △
Notes:
For convenience the class permits chained setters by returning: *this.
The example shown here is based on the example ARXML model in [3] “Compu Method
representing a BITFIELD_TEXTTABLE”
